WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.988
One app, two machines. Pick the one you're on, and Wattzup connects it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.348
What are you training on? The bike and the Stride, each with what Wattzup controls,

00:00:12.348 --> 00:00:13.800
and your last session.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.230
Wattzup keeps looking, and counts the machines nearby.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.780
Your last machine is marked Last used. Pick the bike, and it reads Connecting to

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.379
bike.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.500
Once the bike is connected, setup opens, and the status line says so.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.403
If the Stride isn't answering, its card says what to check, with Try again.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.791
On a phone, the cards stack.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.438
From seven sixty-eight pixels, they sit side by side.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.368
What the tests prove: the server won't switch machines while a ride is running.

00:01:14.568 --> 00:01:18.056
So the dashboard ends the ride first, through the end dialog.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.022
That is journey two. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live training

00:01:27.022 --> 00:01:27.800
display.
